s."},{"text":"Work with government, NGO and community stakeholders."},{"text":"Maintain confidentiality and ethical standards."},{"text":"Evaluate whether community interventions are reaching intended populations."}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong NGO Health Worker profile combines community-health knowledge, field implementation, health education, beneficiary engagement, data collection, program monitoring and digital public-health skills."},{"type":"p","text":"The most valuable progression is to move beyond basic outreach work toward program implementation + data + monitoring & evaluation + community engagement. This combination creates a clear pathway from field-level health work into Public Health Program Officer, M&E Specialist, Program Coordinator and eventually Program Manager or Public Health Specialist roles."}]}]}